# VI. The central channel: unifying a distributed body

Another cluster visualizes energy rising through a central axis, becoming progressively subtler, dissolving above the head, or illuminating an interior void. Dyczkowski’s translations describe increasingly subtle light, ascent through the centres, the opening of the middle, and the manifestation of Bhairava.

Whether or not one accepts a literal subtle anatomy, the phenomenological operation is clear.

The ordinary body is represented as:

[
B_i
===

{b_1,b_2,\ldots,b_n},
]

a distributed field of sensations and action possibilities.

The practice imposes a global axis:

[
\mathcal Z_i:
B_i
\rightarrow
\operatorname{Centralized}(B_i).
]

Then the axis is progressively subtilized:

[
\text{body}
\rightarrow
\text{energy}
\rightarrow
\text{light}
\rightarrow
\text{space}
\rightarrow
\text{supportlessness}.
]

The technique does not merely move an object called energy.

It transforms the **geometry of embodied self-location**.

The practitioner may cease experiencing the self as:

[
\text{a point behind the eyes}
]

and instead experience:

* vertical extension;
* whole-body luminosity;
* central spaciousness;
* disappearance of ordinary bodily boundaries.

The traditional interpretation is ascent of Śakti into Bhairava.

Our neutral interpretation is:

[
\partial S_i
+
\mathcal G_i^{\mathrm{body}}
\rightarrow
\partial S_i'
+
\mathcal G_i'.
]

The represented self-boundary and body geometry change.

That alone does not prove that the subject has become cosmically universal.

